The S7comm and S7CommPlus implementations are Rust code. Parts of the S7CommPlus client
follow the protocol handling of S7CommPlusDriver (Thomas Wiens, LGPL-3.0). Protocol
descriptions used as references:
  - Wireshark s7comm and s7comm-plus dissectors
  - snap7 (Davide Nardella)
  - nodes7 (plcpeople) and node-red-contrib-s7 (address syntax)
  - S7CommPlusDriver (Thomas Wiens)

The binary addon (bin/*/s7napi.node) statically links these Rust crates and their
dependencies: napi, napi-derive, serde_json, chrono, socket2, rustls, ring, aes,
flate2 (zlib-rs). Their licenses (MIT, Apache-2.0, ISC, BSD-style) apply to those parts.

